      <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm p-8 md:p-12 prose prose-lg max-w-none">

        <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Most homeowners in Dover never think about rekeying their locks — until something goes wrong. The truth is, your home's security isn't just about having good locks. It's about controlling who has access to those locks. Rekeying is one of the simplest, most affordable ways to reset that control. Here's everything you need to know.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-10 mb-4">What Does Rekeying Actually Mean?</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Rekeying means changing the internal pins inside your lock cylinder so that the old key no longer works. A locksmith replaces the pins with a new configuration that only a new key can open. The lock hardware itself stays the same — you're just resetting which key operates it.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          This is different from <a href="/services/lock-change/" class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold hover:underline">replacing your locks entirely</a>, which involves new hardware. Rekeying is faster and typically costs much less. Our <a href="/services/lock-rekeying/" class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold hover:underline">lock rekeying service</a> can update all the locks in a typical home in under an hour.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-10 mb-4">7 Situations When You Should Rekey Your Locks</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-8 mb-3">1. You Just Moved Into a New Home</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          This is the number one reason to rekey. When you move into any home — new construction, resale, or rental — you have no idea how many keys to that home exist. Previous owners, contractors, real estate agents, neighbors with spare keys — the list can be long. Rekeying on move-in day is the single best thing you can do for your new home's security.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-8 mb-3">2. After a Break-In or Attempted Break-In</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          If your home was burglarized or someone attempted to break in, rekey or replace your locks immediately. Even if the doors appeared undamaged, a professional burglar can pick or duplicate a key without leaving obvious signs. Don't assume your existing locks are still secure.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-8 mb-3">3. After a Breakup or Roommate Change</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          If someone who previously had a key to your home is no longer someone you trust — an ex-partner, a former roommate, a housekeeping service you no longer use — it's time to rekey. Asking for a key back doesn't guarantee there aren't copies. Rekeying eliminates the uncertainty entirely.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-8 mb-3">4. After Losing a Key</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          A lost house key is a security liability. You don't know who found it or whether they can identify which door it opens. If your keys were lost in a visible location (your own driveway, a nearby parking lot, at work), rekeying is worth serious consideration.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-8 mb-3">5. After Hiring Contractors or Service Workers</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          If you gave a key to a plumber, electrician, house cleaner, or dog walker — even one you trusted — it's good practice to rekey after their work is complete. People change, employment relationships end, and you want to be in control of who can access your home long-term.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-8 mb-3">6. When Your Locks Are Getting Old</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Lock cylinders wear down over time. If your locks are more than 10 years old and you're noticing stiffness, wobble, or the key catching, a rekey won't solve the mechanical issue — that may call for a full <a href="/services/lock-repair/" class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold hover:underline">lock repair</a> or replacement. But if the hardware is still solid, periodic rekeying keeps the key control up to date.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-8 mb-3">7. As Part of an Annual Security Review</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Security-conscious homeowners in Dover and Kent County treat lock rekeying as routine maintenance — similar to changing smoke detector batteries. An annual or bi-annual check with a residential locksmith ensures your locks are performing correctly and that key control is up to date.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mt-10 mb-4">Rekeying vs. Replacing Your Locks — Which Is Right for You?</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Rekeying is the right choice when your lock hardware is in good shape and you simply need to reset key access. It's typically 50–70% less expensive than a full lock replacement.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          You should consider replacing locks when:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 mb-6 space-y-2">
          <li>The lock is damaged, worn, or doesn't function smoothly</li>
          <li>You want to upgrade to a higher-security lock brand</li>
          <li>You're adding a smart lock or keypad entry</li>
          <li>The lock was forced or tampered with during a break-in</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Our <a href="/services/residential-locksmith/" class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold hover:underline">residential locksmith</a> team can assess your locks and recommend the most cost-effective solution for your situation.
        </p>

